id: R10
target: src/sello/ristretto.nim
desc: ristrettoMap: the c CT_SELECT condition inverted, 'feCMove(c, r, not wasSquare)' -> 'feCMove(c, r, wasSquare)' -- selects r exactly when was_square holds (the case RFC 9496 §4.3.4 says c should stay -1), corrupting the numerator N's sign term for every square case. Second instance of RFC-004 slice 8b's "the map's was_square select flip" target, alongside R09.
====OLD====
  feCMove(c, r, not wasSquare)
====NEW====
  feCMove(c, r, wasSquare)
====END====
